1577	      `/dashboard/servers/${server.id}`
1578	    );
1579	    return;
1580	  }
1581	  // DATA SAFETY (critical): a reinstall destroys the VM, and `destroyVm` runs
1582	  // `qm destroy` with { "destroy-unreferenced-disks": 1, purge: 1 } — which wipes
1583	  // EVERY disk the vmid owns, including attached block-storage Volume disks
1584	  // (scsi1+, `vmdata:vm-<vmid>-disk-N`). A disk named `vm-<vmid>-disk-N` is owned
1585	  // by that vmid, and both purge and the default destroy (which removes disks
1586	  // referenced in config, incl. detached `unusedN` entries) delete it; there is no
1587	  // Proxmox API to selectively spare it, and the reinstall re-clones onto the SAME
1588	  // vmid, so we cannot GUARANTEE such a disk survives the destroy. Rather than risk
1589	  // wiping a customer's data, BLOCK the reinstall until the volume(s) are detached.
1590	  // Detaching moves the disk to an "unused" entry (data preserved on storage) and it
1591	  // can be re-attached after the reinstall. This runs BEFORE any status change or
1592	  // destructive call, so a blocked reinstall touches nothing.
1593	  //
1594	  // Match on `serverId` ALONE — NOT `status: "ATTACHED"`. Detaching keeps
