2003	      // content back — including whatever /etc/shadow existed when it was
2004	      // taken — which can hold an older password than Server.rootPasswordEnc
2005	      // if a PASSWORD_RESET (or anything else) changed it since the snapshot
2006	      // was created. Left alone, every later SSH from the platform would
2007	      // authenticate with the DB's (now wrong) password against the guest's
2008	      // reverted (now correct-for-the-snapshot) one — the exact "All
